Z||000000||Vlad||01-23-2001||01:10 AM||||Well......<P>My GT never had a great gas mileage, but now something seems to be wrong.<BR>It generally comes to 15-18 mpg, but fuel consumption is sort of uneven.<BR>Sometimes I make on first 1/3 of the tank about 100 km (which is good), but the rest goes like creasy and I can hardly make another 100 km. Or sometimes, the situation just an opposite. <BR>No codes.<P>Any advise would be highly appreciated.<P>85 GT Auto||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||01-23-2001||01:50 AM||||200 miles to the tank for an auto is just about the norm. I don't rely on what the gauge says very much, I just know the range. My V-6 autos get around 18 MPG.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||01-23-2001||02:03 AM||||Sorry, but those are km, not miles. <P>200 km about 145 miles.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||01-23-2001||04:15 AM||||Well, the Fiero's gas gauge was never the most accurate thing in the world...  <P>I'd give your car a quick tune up (plugs, dist. cap, wires, etc) and run a bottle of fuel system cleaner/carbon remover through there.  I'm averaging about 20mpg with my 86 GT 5 speed, but my gas gauge doesn't work..||||reg||1
